-- Conversion of a paperless-ngx 2.20 database to the v3.0 state (followed by
-- catchup-v3.0.0-v3.4.2.sql) on PostgreSQL, without Python.
--
-- Source: upstream v3.4.2 `src/{documents,paperless,paperless_mail}/migrations/*` – exactly the
-- migrations that `manage.py migrate --plan` of v3.4.2 runs on a 2.20.15 database
-- (0001_squashed/0002_squashed/paperless_mail.0001_squashed count as applied there, because all
-- replaced 2.x migrations are applied). SQL generated with Django 5.2.18 (schema_editor
-- collect_sql, like `sqlmigrate`) from the reference venv: tests/dbmigrate/gen_catchup_v2.py.
-- RunPython steps are translated by hand and marked. Two of them need Rust instead of SQL
-- (line `-- @rust <name>`, see crates/pl-dbmigrate/src/catchup.rs):
--   sha256_checksums        documents.0016 reads every original/archive file (SHA-256 instead of MD5)
--   fulltext_query_prefixes documents.0017 regex with lookbehind like Python `re`
-- documents.1075 comes from v2.20.15 (missing in 2.19.x and 2.20.0 … 2.20.4).
--
-- Format like catchup-v3.0.0-v3.4.2.sql: every step begins with `-- @@ <app> <name>`; applied
-- in file order, only steps whose row is missing in django_migrations. The transaction
-- runs with `SET CONSTRAINTS ALL IMMEDIATE` (instead of Django's `atomic = False` in
-- paperless_mail.0002): no open foreign key checks before ALTER TABLE.

